Subject: AlienHand Work Justification

Description: SOP description of the justification step, called "jusitification" by the user, for matching actual work performed to the specification requirements that warranted the work. This artifact is a behavior note for future work and a current ledger of completed project changes.

@ [source] platform/source/SOP_Markdown.md
@ [source] platform/source/Subject-Driven_Design.md
@ [source] platform/Delineation.sop
@ [source] platform/Integration.sop
@ [specification] AlienHand/docs/irc-chat-platform.sop
@ [foundation] AlienHand/docs/irc-chat-foundation.md

& [WorkJustification] is the accountability pass that connects implemented work to the specification requirement that called for it
  + [user_term] is "jusitification"
  + [canonical_term] is justification
  + [implemented_work] is an artifact, code path, dependency, configuration, document, test, or committed change that exists in the repository
  + [spec_requirement] is the SOP subject, directive, constraint, or progress node that warranted the work
  + [evidence] is an inspectable file, git commit, submodule state, command result, or test result
  + [verification] is the check that confirms the work matches the requirement
  + [unresolved] is any remainder that prevents claiming full completion
  + [resolution] is justified, partially_justified, specified_only, blocked, or rejected

  = must: distinguish implemented work from planned work
  = must: map each work claim to at least one [spec_requirement]
  = must: preserve evidence for each claim
  = must: preserve unresolved gaps instead of converting them into completion language
  = must: update this layer when substantial work changes the project state
  - never: claim a feature is implemented merely because it is specified
  - never: hide missing verification behind a broad summary

## Justification Entry Schema

& [JustificationEntry] is one auditable mapping from work performed to requirement satisfied
  + [work_id] is a stable local identifier for the work entry
  + [work_type] is dependency, documentation, protocol, runtime_code, test, configuration, or verification
  + [requirement_anchor] is the specification subject or directive that required the work
  + [implemented_artifact] is the repository artifact that now exists
  + [evidence_anchor] is the file path, commit, command, or observation supporting the claim
  + [verification_result] is what was checked
  + [status] is justified, partially_justified, specified_only, blocked, or rejected
  + [uncertainty] is the honest remainder

  = must: be specific enough that a future pass can inspect the claim
  = must: use [specified_only] when a runtime behavior is only described by a requirement document and does not yet exist
  = must: use [partially_justified] when work exists but implementation or verification is incomplete

## Current Work Ledger

